The rocks is a list of 5, 10, and -5.
The last is the last position of rocks.
The stack is an empty list of whole numbers.
For each rock in rocks.
If rock is more than 0, Place rock into stack.
If rock is less than 0.
The alive is 1.
Repeat while alive is 1.
The end is the last position of stack.
If end is less than 0, Place rock into stack, set alive to 0, stop.
The top is item end of stack.
If top is less than 0, Place rock into stack, set alive to 0, stop.
The size is 0 minus rock.
If top is less than size, remove the last item from stack.
If top is more than size, set alive to 0, stop.
If top is size, remove the last item from stack, set alive to 0, stop.


The line is empty text.
For each rock in stack.
If the length of line is more than 0, Place "," into line.
Place format whole number rock as text into line.

Show line.
